---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Section from "../components/layout/Section.astro";
import Container from "../components/layout/Container.astro";
import Footer from "../components/layout/Footer.astro";
import ClassifiedBand from "../components/ui/ClassifiedBand.astro";
import Eyebrow from "../components/typography/Eyebrow.astro";
import Heading from "../components/typography/Heading.astro";
import Rule from "../components/typography/Rule.astro";
import PitchDeckNav from "@/components/ui/PitchDeckNav.astro";
import "@/styles/global.css";
---

<Layout title="MI5 Monitoring Station — Core Frequency Anomaly">
  <ClassifiedBand
    label="TOP SECRET — MI5 MONITORING STATION // CORE FREQUENCY ANOMALY"
  />

  <!-- ─── PAGE HEADER ─── -->
  <Section variant="black" spacing="md">
    <Container>
      <Eyebrow>Central Collision</Eyebrow>
      <Heading level={2} variant="section">The <em>Battleground</em></Heading>
      <Rule />
      <p class="prose page-intro">
        The ultimate absurd ideological showdown. Working-class chaos against
        centuries of royal choreography. A rebellion that isn't really a
        rebellion. An institution that isn't even paying attention.
      </p>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <!-- ─── MONITORING STATION HEADER ─── -->
  <div class="monitoring-band">
    <pre
      class="monitoring-header">
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MI5 MONITORING STATION // CORE FREQUENCY ANOMALY
THE REBELLION VS. THE CROWN
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    </pre>
  </div>

  <!-- ─── SPLIT-SCREEN COLLISION ─── -->
  <div class="collision-grid">
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- JOHN LENNON — LEFT -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <div class="collision-panel collision-panel--lennon">
      <div class="collision-badge">THE REBELLION</div>

      <!-- Surveillance-style image -->
      <div class="photo-frame">
        <img
          class="portrait-photo"
          src="/john.jpg"
          alt="John Lennon — 1965"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <div class="tape-overlay" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="photo-label">ABBEY ROAD // RECORDING TAPE BOX</div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="collision-name">
        JOHN LENNON <span class="collision-subtitle"
          >// The Unintentional Anarchist</span
        >
      </h3>

      <blockquote class="collision-quote">
        "We are where we are, lads. Best be relaxed. We're about to get medals.
        I mean, they're honors for pop music. It's not like we actually had to
        kill anyone to get them."
      </blockquote>

      <div class="profile-section">
        <span class="section-label">The Stance</span>
        <p>
          Slouching, irreverent, and chemically relaxed. Armed with a
          working-class Liverpool wit, a packed joint in his velvet jacket
          pocket, and an instinctive disdain for institutional pretension.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="profile-section">
        <span class="section-label">The Threat Profile</span>
        <p>
          <strong>High Cultural Authority.</strong> John isn't trying to overthrow
          the government; he's just naturally skeptical of royal pomp. But to a rigid
          establishment, his casual, effortless influence over millions of youth makes
          him look more dangerous than an army of foreign agents.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="profile-section">
        <span class="section-label">The Trajectory</span>
        <p>
          Stumbles into a multi-year psychological war he doesn't know he's
          fighting. Every time MI5 tries to subtle-sabotage him, his music just
          gets sharper, weirder, and more radicalized — culminating in the
          ultimate act of defiance: returning his actual MBE medal to Buckingham
          Palace.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="profile-section">
        <span class="section-label">The Comedy DNA</span>
        <ul class="agent-list">
          <li>
            <strong>The Unwitting Catalyst:</strong> John's "killing people" comment
            at the MBE ceremony is pure working-class irreverence, not calculated
            political protest. He has no idea he just made the most powerful enemy
            of his life.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The Inverse Feedback Loop:</strong> Every MI5 manipulation designed
            to destroy him — the "Jesus" controversy amplification, the media hostility,
            the institutional pressure — pushes him further into radicalization. The
            conspiracy creates the very threat it was designed to neutralize.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The Accidental Radical:</strong> His genuine political awakening
            — driven by authentic conviction and primal therapy — is also partially
            the product of the very conspiracy designed to destroy him. Dramatic irony
            as the engine of tragedy.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="profile-section">
        <span class="section-label">The Internal Conflict</span>
        <p>
          Torn between his desire for peace and his naturally combative
          personality. He preaches love and understanding while being quick to
          anger and harsh judgment. This contradiction makes him vulnerable — he
          genuinely wants to make the world better but his methods often
          alienate the very people he needs to reach. He's caught between
          loyalty to The Beatles (his artistic family) and his growing need for
          individual expression. Every choice that serves his personal growth
          seems to damage the band, creating guilt he masks with defiance.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="profile-section">
        <span class="section-label">The Vulnerabilities</span>
        <p>
          Abandonment anxiety (father left, mother died, band fracturing).
          Impostor syndrome despite massive success. Susceptible to paranoia
          when under pressure. Self-destructive tendencies when feeling trapped.
          And a deep-seated need for authenticity in an increasingly artificial
          world — a need that makes him both impossible to control and
          dangerously predictable to those who understand it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="profile-section">
        <span class="section-label">The Narrative Arc — Three Acts</span>
        <ul class="agent-list">
          <li>
            <strong>1965 — The Unwitting Catalyst:</strong> John's casual "killing
            people" quip at the MBE ceremony is pure instinct, not rebellion. He's
            uncomfortable with royal formality but hasn't yet developed the political
            consciousness that will define his later years. His casual disrespect
            unknowingly triggers Philip's five-year vendetta.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>1968 — The Manipulated Radical:</strong> Operation Minuet's psychological
            campaign amplifies every controversy around him. The "Jesus" firestorm,
            media hostility, institutional pressure — all orchestrated or amplified
            by MI5. His growing political awareness is genuine but partially manufactured.
            He becomes the radical Philip needs him to be.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>1970 — The Defiant Survivor:</strong> Returns his MBE. Survives
            an assassination attempt he never knows about. The Beatles dissolve through
            their own dynamics, not Philip's design. He walks away free, never learning
            how close he came to death or that his political journey was partially
            a puppet show. Survival as victory.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- THE QUEEN — RIGHT -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <div class="collision-panel collision-panel--queen">
      <div class="collision-badge collision-badge--right">THE CROWN</div>

      <!-- Formal portrait-style image -->
      <div class="photo-frame photo-frame--queen">
        <img
          class="portrait-photo portrait-photo--queen"
          src="/queen.jpg"
          alt="Her Majesty The Queen — Official Portrait"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <div class="royal-border" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="photo-label photo-label--queen">
          BUCKINGHAM PALACE // OFFICIAL PORTRAIT
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="collision-name collision-name--queen">
        HER MAJESTY THE QUEEN <span class="collision-subtitle"
          >// The Oblivious Institution</span
        >
      </h3>

      <blockquote class="collision-quote collision-quote--queen">
        "They seem like very polite young men, Philip. The short one with the
        drums has a lovely smile. Do stop pacing, you're making the corgis
        anxious."
      </blockquote>

      <div class="profile-section">
        <span class="section-label">The Stance</span>
        <p>
          Perfectly poised, completely unbothered, and utterly detached from the
          panic brewing in her own basement. Armed with inherited centuries of
          tradition, absolute social grace, and a genuine indifference to
          rock-and-roll.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="profile-section">
        <span class="section-label">The Threat Profile</span>
        <p>
          <strong>Absolute Institutional Weight.</strong> She represents the massive,
          immovable iceberg of the British Empire. She doesn't dislike the Beatles;
          she graciously hands them their medals because her Prime Minister told her
          to.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="profile-section">
        <span class="section-label">The Grand Satirical Irony</span>
        <p>
          The Queen is the epic center of the show's cosmic joke. While Prince
          Philip uses the entire apparatus of MI5 to protect her honor from
          Lennon's "rebellion," Her Majesty remains blissfully unaware of the
          multi-million dollar conspiracy operating in her name. She treats the
          Beatles like a passing weather system, entirely blind to the fact that
          her husband has turned her palace into a paranoid cold-war command
          center.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="profile-section">
        <span class="section-label">The Comedy DNA</span>
        <ul class="agent-list">
          <li>
            <strong>The Oblivious Iceberg:</strong> The Queen is the massive, immovable
            institution — while Philip rages and Mountbatten schemes downstairs, she's
            signing state papers and asking about the corgis. The entire conspiracy
            operates in a building whose owner has no idea it exists.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The Flat Arc:</strong> She maintains absolute consistency while
            everyone around her spirals. Her presence at Committee meetings serves
            as both legitimacy and restraint — she contributes hilariously mundane
            counterpoints to Mountbatten's psychological warfare briefings (questioning
            budgets, suggesting tea service protocols).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The Final Judgment:</strong> Her one scene of moral weight — a
            look, not a speech — delivers the series' verdict. Patience defeats everything.
            The institution endures not by acting, but by refusing to.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="profile-section">
        <span class="section-label">The Motivation</span>
        <p>
          Her overriding motivation is <strong
            >institutional preservation</strong
          >. She views the monarchy as a thousand-year institution that must
          outlast any individual crisis, including her husband's wounded pride.
          John's 1965 comment is, to her, a momentary irritation that will be
          forgotten if ignored, but could become a lasting scandal if
          mishandled. Her secondary motivation is managing Philip's escalating
          obsession — by participating in the Committee, she hopes to moderate
          his impulses and prevent actions that could genuinely threaten the
          Crown.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="profile-section">
        <span class="section-label">The Internal Conflict</span>
        <p>
          Torn between duty to her husband and duty to the Crown. She is loyal
          to Philip and feels a deep, if formal, affection for him. But his
          Operation Minuet runs counter to her every instinct for caution and
          stability. Every time she reluctantly sanctions a part of his plan,
          she weighs the risk of indulging his folly against the risk of
          directly opposing him and causing a domestic crisis. She is a
          fundamentally conservative individual forced to oversee a radically
          unconventional and undignified operation. Her struggle is to maintain
          the dignity of her office while being party to something utterly
          lacking in it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="profile-section">
        <span class="section-label">The Narrative Arc — Three Acts</span>
        <ul class="agent-list">
          <li>
            <strong>1965 — The Cautious Voice:</strong> Witnesses John's comment with
            diplomatic composure. When Philip convenes the Committee, she participates
            reluctantly, hoping her presence will moderate his response. "He's an
            artist, Philip. They're meant to be dramatic."
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>1968 — The Reluctant Moderator:</strong> Serves as the Committee's
            conscience. Her contributions are hilariously mundane — questioning budgets,
            suggesting protocol. Watches Philip's growing obsession with increasing
            concern.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>1970 — The Vindicated Survivor:</strong> John's MBE return triggers
            Philip's assassination demand. Her horror represents her moral line. When
            the plot collapses into farce, her reaction is weary vindication. Her
            final look to Philip reaffirms: institutions endure by staying above personal
            vendettas.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ─── CENTER OVERLAP STAMP ─── -->
    <div class="center-stamp" aria-hidden="true">
      CULTURAL CONTAGION DIRECTIVE<br />
      <span class="stamp-sub">DO NOT CROSS FILE</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ─── DIAGNOSTIC SUMMARY ─────────── -->
  <Section variant="paper" spacing="lg">
    <Container>
      <Eyebrow>Diagnostic Summary</Eyebrow>
      <Heading level={2} variant="section"
        >The Anatomy of an <em>Irreverent Farce</em></Heading
      >
      <Rule />

      <div class="diagnostic-band">
        <pre
          class="diagnostic-header">
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DIAGNOSTIC SUMMARY // THE ANATOMY OF AN IRREVERENT FARCE
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        </pre>
      </div>

      <h4 class="diag-subhead">The Ideological Cold War</h4>

      <p class="prose">
        This is the comedy of <strong>asymmetric warfare</strong>.
      </p>

      <div class="asymmetric-grid">
        <div class="asymmetric-item">
          <span class="asymmetric-char asymmetric-char--lennon">Lennon</span>
          <p>
            fights a very loud, very public battle against the concept of "The
            Establishment."
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="asymmetric-item">
          <span class="asymmetric-char asymmetric-char--queen">The Queen</span>
          <p>
            <em>is</em> the establishment, but she is too busy reviewing state paperwork
            and managing royal lineages to notice his protest.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="prose">
        The real conflict is fought entirely in the shadow between them. Prince
        Philip and his bumbling agents treat a pop band's lyrics like a matter
        of imperial national security, launching a secret war against a
        counter-culture movement that doesn't even know it's under attack. It is
        the ultimate collision of working-class chaos against centuries of royal
        choreography.
      </p>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <PitchDeckNav current="/collision" />
  <!-- ─── FOOTER ─── -->
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ─── PAGE INTRO ─── */
  .page-intro {
    max-width: 650px;
    color: var(--text5);
    font-size: var(--fs4);
    margin: var(--space-1);
  }

  /* ─── MONITORING BAND ─── */
  .monitoring-band {
    background: var(--bg);
    padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-5);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--bg4);
  }

  .monitoring-header {
    max-width: var(--container-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    letter-spacing: 0.04rem;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* ─── COLLISION GRID ─── */
  .collision-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* ─── COLLISION PANEL ─── */
  .collision-panel {
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-5);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .collision-panel--lennon {
    background: var(--bg2);
    border-right: 2px solid var(--bg);
  }

  .collision-panel--queen {
    background: var(--bg1);
  }

  .collision-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs1);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.2rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 4px 12px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent-blue);
    color: var(--accent-blue);
  }

  .collision-badge--right {
    border-color: var(--color-amber);
    color: var(--color-amber);
  }

  /* ─── PHOTO FRAMES ─── */
  .photo-frame {
    position: relative;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--bg4);
  }

  .portrait-photo {
    width: 100%;
    height: 500px;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .portrait-photo--queen {
    filter: saturate(1.1) contrast(1.05);
    object-position: center 20%;
  }

  .tape-overlay {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(
      0deg,
      transparent,
      transparent 40px,
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.03) 40px,
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.03) 42px
    );
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .royal-border {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    border: 8px solid rgba(200, 168, 75, 0.15);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .photo-label {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: var(--space-2);
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    background: #111;
    color: #888;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs1);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.15rem;
    padding: 4px 12px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border: 1px solid #333;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .photo-label--queen {
    background: #1a1520;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    border-color: rgba(200, 168, 75, 0.3);
  }

  /* ─── COLLISION NAMES ─── */
  .collision-name {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.5vw, 1.8rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text1);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
    letter-spacing: 0.02rem;
  }

  .collision-name--queen {
    color: var(--color-cream);
  }

  .collision-subtitle {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    letter-spacing: 0.06rem;
    display: block;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .collision-name--queen .collision-subtitle {
    color: var(--color-amber);
  }

  /* ─── QUOTES ─── */
  .collision-quote {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-blue);
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    margin: var(--space-3) 0;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text4);
    background: var(--accent-blue-subtle);
  }

  .collision-quote--queen {
    border-left-color: var(--color-amber);
    background: rgba(138, 110, 42, 0.06);
    color: var(--text5);
    padding-right: 3rem;
    margin-right: 3rem;
  }

  /* ─── PROFILE SECTIONS ─── */
  .profile-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .section-label {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs2);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.2rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-faint);
    padding-bottom: 2px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .collision-panel--queen .section-label {
    color: var(--color-amber);
  }

  .profile-section p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--fs3);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text5);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .profile-section strong {
    color: var(--text3);
  }

  /* ─── AGENT LIST STYLES (shared with mi5/establishment) ─── */
  .agent-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .agent-list li {
    font-size: var(--fs3);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--text5);
    padding: var(--space-1) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-faint);
  }

  .agent-list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .agent-list li strong {
    color: var(--text3);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /* ─── CENTER STAMP ─── */
  .center-stamp {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(-15deg);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: 0.2rem;
    text-align: center;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    line-height: 1.4;
    padding: 12px 24px;
    border: 3px solid var(--color-red);
    color: var(--color-red);
    background: rgba(139, 26, 26, 0.08);
    z-index: 10;
    pointer-events: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .stamp-sub {
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.3rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  /* ─── DIAGNOSTIC SECTION ─── */
  .diagnostic-band {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
  }

  .diagnostic-header {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.04rem;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-faint);
    padding: var(--space-3);
    background: var(--bg2);
  }

  .diag-subhead {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text2);
    margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  .asymmetric-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin: var(--space-5) 0;
  }

  .asymmetric-item {
    background: var(--bg2);
    padding: var(--space-4);
  }

  .asymmetric-item:first-child {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue);
  }

  .asymmetric-item:last-child {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-amber);
  }

  .asymmetric-char {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.2rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .asymmetric-char--lennon {
    color: var(--accent-blue);
  }

  .asymmetric-char--queen {
    color: var(--color-amber);
  }

  .asymmetric-item p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text5);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ─── RESPONSIVE ─── */
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .collision-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .collision-panel--lennon {
      border-right: none;
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--bg);
    }

    .center-stamp {
      position: relative;
      top: auto;
      left: auto;
      transform: rotate(-8deg);
      margin: var(--space-4);
      font-size: 0.7rem;
    }

    .asymmetric-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .photo-label {
      font-size: 0.45rem;
      white-space: normal;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .center-stamp {
      transform: rotate(-5deg);
      font-size: 0.6rem;
      padding: 8px 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
